# markdown-table-cells fixtures

These are `*.md.fixture`, NOT `*.md`, and that is load-bearing twice over:
`checks/markdown-scan.nix` scans every tracked `.md` in the tree, and the
`markdown-table-cells` hook runs on every tracked `.md` — so a `.md` fixture
carrying a deliberately broken table would fail the very check it exists to
test. treefmt would also reformat the exact cell counts each one encodes.

Each fixture states what it proves and the exact hits it expects. The suite's
job is NOT "the linters find bugs" — it is the DISJOINTNESS claim that
justifies carrying two of them, which is the thing that can rot silently when
either tool updates.
